{"id": "gsm8k:591", "benchmark": "gsm8k", "started_unix": 1790749525.2664716, "first_event_seconds": 1.2177285819780082, "wall_seconds": 11.289521080965642, "prompt_sha256": "b325453bba958b796ceffa32c94af4dc85815ce182e913ceac5ce28581b7416f", "prompt_tokens": 169, "max_new_tokens": 256, "completion_tokens": 214, "finish_reason": {"type": "stop", "matched": 151645}, "request_id": "2b8438e3cea94d2d9af5ac5124714233", "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. The first dog is an Affenpinscher, who weighs 10 pounds.\n2. The next dog is a Dachshund, who weighs twice as much as the Affenpinscher. Therefore, the Dachshund weighs:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 10 = 20 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n3. The next dog is a Papillon, who weighs one-fourth as much as the Dachshund. Therefore, the Papillon weighs:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{20}{4} = 5 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n4. The last dog is a Mastiff, who weighs 44 times the weight of the Papillon. Therefore, the Mastiff weighs:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 5 = 220 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the weight of the Mastiff is \\(\\boxed{220}\\) pounds.", "final_answer": null, "gold_answer": "220", "truncated": false, "events": 214, "arm": "full", "dataset_sha256": "69354b6d9f93ee5e7eaf15b9314f2fb5f0ad10819613fc4cc16c37bbe798d56d"}
